    51	
    52	## Shared CandidateDiscovery contract cases
    53	
    54	The offline tests exercise the real `LocalEmbeddingCandidateDiscovery.discover` boundary; only the
    55	`EmbeddingRuntime.embed` implementation is substituted. The live run replaces that substitution
    56	with `OnnxEmbeddingRuntime` and reuses the same cases.
    57	
    58	| Case | Test selector | Independent input/expectation |
    59	|---|---|---|
    60	| Port identity and no write surface | `test_provider_satisfies_the_port_and_has_no_write_surface` | Provider satisfies `CandidateDiscovery`; no accept/reject/write vocabulary |
    61	| Ranking and relation filters | `test_contract_ranks_and_filters` | `SCN-001` gives a nonempty ranked list; source ids equal the requested id; `implemented_by` selects sources, `exercised_by` selects tests, `verified_by` selects nothing |
    62	| `top_k` trimming | `test_top_k_and_rank_trimming` | `top_k=1` yields one candidate at rank 1; `top_k=0` is rejected |
    63	| Requirement and source behavior | `test_requirement_discovery_and_source_no_candidates` | `REQ-001` proposes scenarios; `CODE-001` returns an empty list |
    64	| Index binding | `test_index_binding_tracks_content_and_model` | binding is `sha256`; baseline-a and baseline-b differ |
    65	| No mutation | `test_discovery_does_not_write_links_evidence_or_findings` | accepted links, evidence, and findings are byte-equal before/after |
    66	| Malformed output | `test_malformed_embedding_is_a_typed_failure` | non-finite vector → `RetrievalUnavailable`, no partial list |
    67	| Remote endpoint | `test_remote_endpoint_is_refused_before_any_connection`, `test_remote_endpoint_route_is_a_400` | `InvalidRequest`/400 before a connection |
    68	| Missing weights | `test_missing_model_directory_is_unavailable`, `test_onnx_runtime_refuses_missing_weights`, `test_missing_model_route_is_a_503` | `RetrievalUnavailable`/503, no download |
    69	| Default remains fake | `test_default_registry_does_not_include_local` | effective registry is `["fake"]` without opt-in |
    70	
    71	The canonical `SCN-3204` scenario additionally requires a known artifact with no eligible targets
    72	to return an empty list while the API response retains provider/model/index provenance, and a
    73	runtime that cannot report its model identity to fail explicitly rather than invent one.
    74	
